### Post-rollback verification (after old pods fully terminated)
$ kubectl get pods -l app=lab2-app -o jsonpath image field
lab2-app-88f4c9fc9-bv4qd: devops-lab2-app:2.0.0
lab2-app-88f4c9fc9-snrr5: devops-lab2-app:2.0.0

$ curl http://192.168.49.2:30080/health
{"status":"UP","version":"2.0.0"}


# OBSERVATION: the curl taken immediately after 'rollout undo' returned 2.0.1
# because the terminating 2.0.1 pods were still registered in the service
# endpoints for a few seconds. Once they finished terminating, the service
# served only 2.0.0 pods. Zero-downtime is preserved during this overlap.
